.SH NAME
.PP
createSchema \- create a Schema
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]db.createSchema(<name>, <schemaDef>)\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Sdb
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to create a Schema and specify the field definitions of
the Schema.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \[bu] 2
name ( \f[I]string, required\f[] )
.RS 2
.PP
The name of the Schema.
Users needs to ensure that it is globally unique.
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
schemaDef ( \f[I]object, required\f[] )
.RS 2
.PP
Modify the field definition of Schema through the parameter "schemaDef", the
format is
\f[C]{<Name1>: {<field definition>}, <Name2>: {field definition}, ...}\f[]:
.IP \[bu] 2
Name ( \f[I]string\f[] ): Field name.
.RS 2
.PP
Format: \f[C]{"id": {}}\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
Type ( \f[I]string\f[] ): Data type of the field.
.RS 2
.PP
Format: \f[C]{"id": {Type: "int32"}}\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
ReadDefault ( \f[I]The type corresponds to the value of the field "Type"\f[] ):
Read default value.
This parameter is optional.
.RS 2
.PP
Read data through "Information Schema", and the default value to be returned
when the specified field does not exist in the record.
.PP
Format: \f[C]{"id": {Type: "int32", ReadDefault: 0}}\f[]
.RE
.IP \[bu] 2
WriteDefault ( \f[I]The type corresponds to the value of the field "Type"\f[] ):
Write default value.
This parameter is optional.
.RS 2
.PP
Write data through "Information Schema", and the default value that needs to be
supplemented when the specified field does not exist in the written record.
.PP
Format: \f[C]{"id": {Type: "int32", WriteDefault: 0}}\f[]
.RE
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return an object of type
SdbInfoSchema.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
